## Git in this repository (shared by several agents)

Several AI agents work in this repository at the same time.

- Commit ONLY the files you changed, in one step:
  `git flock-commit -m "<message>" -- <file> [<file>...]`
- Run every other git command that writes (pull, push, merge, rebase, stash,
  switch, checkout, reset, tag, branch) through the lock:
  `git flock <command> ...`
- Never run plain `git add` or `git commit`, and never `git commit -a`,
  `git add -A` or `git add .` — they sweep other agents' work into your commit.
- If `git status` shows changes you did not make, leave them alone.
- If a git-flock command exits 75, the repository was busy for 5 minutes;
  wait a moment and retry.
